## Description

This function has arguments with rich, nested Markdown-relevant content.

## Usage

```r
arguments_rich(x, method, describe_arg, table_arg, pre_only, pre_with_intro,
  backtick_code, fence_collision, cr_break, multi_paragraph,
  itemize_multi_paragraph, ...)
```

## Arguments

+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| Argument                  | Description                                                  |
+===========================+==============================================================+
| `x`                       | A basic argument for comparison.                             |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `method`                  | The method to use, described as a nested list:               |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | - `"a"`: Use method A, the default.                          |
|                           | - `"b"`: Use method B instead.                               |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `describe_arg`            | The method to use, described with a definition list:         |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | "a"                                                          |
|                           | :   Use method A.                                            |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | "b"                                                          |
|                           | :   Use method B.                                            |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `table_arg`               | The argument. See the table:                                 |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | |   Col1  |  Col2  |                                         |
|                           | |:---|:---|                                                  |
|                           | |   a  |  1  |                                               |
|                           | |   b  |  2  |                                               |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `pre_only`                | ```                                                          |
|                           | result <- foo(x)                                             |
|                           | print(result)                                                |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | ```                                                          |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `pre_with_intro`          | Example usage:                                               |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | ```                                                          |
|                           | result <- foo(x)                                             |
|                           | print(result)                                                |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | ```                                                          |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `backtick_code`           | Use `` `a` `` or ``` ``nested`` ``` for non-syntactic names. |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `fence_collision`         | Code containing a fence-like line:                           |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | ````                                                         |
|                           | ```r                                                         |
|                           | x <- 1                                                       |
|                           | ```                                                          |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | ````                                                         |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `cr_break`                | First line.                                                  |
|                           | \- hyphen.                                                   |
|                           | \* asterisk.                                                 |
|                           | \+ plus.                                                     |
|                           | 1\. ordered period.                                          |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `` `a` ``                 | A non-syntactic argument name with single backticks.         |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| ``` ``b`` ```             | A label with a double-backtick run.                          |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `multi_paragraph`         | First paragraph.                                             |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | Second paragraph of the description.                         |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+
| `itemize_multi_paragraph` | Options:                                                     |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | - First paragraph.                                           |
|                           |                                                              |
|                           | Second paragraph of this item.                               |
|                           | - Another item.                                              |
+---------------------------+--------------------------------------------------------------+

## Value

Nothing of interest.

## Examples

```{r}
arguments_rich(1, "a", "a", NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, "x", "y")
```
